# P2P Plant Selling and Exchange Feature

This plan outlines the implementation of a peer-to-peer (P2P) marketplace and exchange system within the Leaf-Life application. Users will be able to list their plants for sale or exchange, and other users can send requests to buy or swap.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Renaming Existing "Community" Link**: The current sidebar link labeled "Community" points to the Rewards page. I propose renaming this link to "Rewards" and creating a new "Community" link that leads to the actual P2P Exchange Hub.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Manual Verification**: After implementation, testing will require two separate user accounts to demonstrate the request-and-accept flow.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Projects/Leaf-Life%20-%20Copy/Backend/server.js)
- Update `initDB` to:
    - Add `seller_id` (INT), `listing_type` (VARCHAR), `is_listed` (TINYINT) to `plants` table.
    - Create `trade_requests` table to track P2P transactions.
- Add New Endpoints:
    - `POST /api/marketplace/list`: Mark a user's plant as listed for sale/exchange.
    - `GET /api/marketplace/community`: Fetch all user-listed plants.
    - `GET /api/community/users`: Fetch other users on the platform.
    - `POST /api/trade/request`: Create a buy or exchange request.
    - `GET /api/trade/requests/:userId`: Fetch incoming and outgoing trade requests.
    - `POST /api/trade/respond`: Accept or reject a trade request.

